+
+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** AI reference-checking v1 (issue #548, story RC1.1) has no schema or write path for its evidence foundation: the applicant's explicit referee-contact choice is not recorded, and the applicant-submission IP/UA comparator that later fraud signals (RC3.7) are computed against is not captured.
+
+**Approach:** Two expand-only migrations (`reference_contact_attestation` enum value; `application.submitted_ip_text`/`submitted_user_agent`/`reference_contact_choice` columns), then wire the submission path: `validate_form` requires an explicit attested/declined choice, the transaction writes IP/UA + choice onto the application row, and `insert_acknowledgement_records` gains its fourth write (`reference_contact_attestation`, current `policy_version`) only when attested.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Attestation/acknowledgement vocabulary only — the word "consent" never appears in relation to this record in code, copy, or comments (AD-2 §3.2). (The pre-existing enum type name `consent_type` stays as-is; it is the type name, not the record's vocabulary.)
+- Enum migration follows the `20260420000003` precedent exactly: `ALTER TYPE consent_type ADD VALUE IF NOT EXISTS 'reference_contact_attestation';`
+- Capture columns follow the `cookie_consent_log` precedent: `TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '' CHECK (length(...) <= 64)` / `<= 512`. `reference_contact_choice TEXT` nullable, `CHECK (reference_contact_choice IN ('attested','declined'))` (A4 — pre-v1 rows stay NULL).
+- IP via `request_helpers.client_ip(req)`, UA via `request_helpers.client_user_agent(req)` — both already bounded; extraction happens in `process_form_submission`, values threaded down to the insert.
+- Attestation row writes inside the existing `pog.transaction` via `insert_acknowledgement_records` (AD-2), stamped with `compliance.policy_version`, only when choice = attested. Declined writes NO row and submits normally.
+- Choice is written to `reference_contact_choice` on every successful submission ('attested' or 'declined'), matching the explicit choice.
+- Missing, empty, or tampered choice fails `validate_form` (explicit choice required — no silent skip, no default). Error copy: "Choose one option to continue." (UX §5.3 verbatim — RC1.2's scroll target).
+- Squirrel workflow is mandatory: edit `.sql` files, then `bash run_squirrel.sh` — never hand-edit generated `sql.gleam`.
+- Migrations expand-only, idempotent (`IF NOT EXISTS`).
+
+**Ask First:**
+- Any change outside the Code Map files (e.g. if a shared-file collision with the parallel RC2.1 minion appears — `shared/src/shared/reference_call.gleam` is theirs).
+
+**Never:**
+- No UI/card/copy/framing work — that is story RC1.2 (`form_sections/`, `form_pages.gleam`, `form_copy.gleam`, `form_fields.gleam` stay untouched).
+- Never expose `submitted_ip_text` / `submitted_user_agent` on any API payload, log line, or landlord-visible surface (AD-11: internal-only). Only `reference_contact_choice` joins the shared type/payload (A4).
+- No `reference_call`/`reference_objection_log` schema (RC2.1, parallel minion), no fraud-signal computation (RC3.7), no auto-reject.
+- No backfill of attestation rows for pre-v1 applications.
+- Never merge the PR; never commit env files/secrets.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Attested submission | `reference_contact_choice=attested` | App row: choice='attested', IP/UA stored; 3rd ack row type `reference_contact_attestation` with `policy_version` (2→3 rows no-guarantor) | N/A |
+| Declined submission | `reference_contact_choice=declined` | App row: choice='declined', IP/UA stored; NO attestation row; submission succeeds normally | N/A |
+| Missing choice | field absent/empty | `validate_form` error on `reference_contact_choice`; form re-renders; zero app/ack rows persisted | Validation error "Choose one option to continue." |
+| Tampered choice | value not in {attested, declined} | Same as missing (validation rejects); if it ever reached the insert layer, tx aborts loudly (`HandlerLogicError`) | 500 + log, never a coerced value |
+| No IP/UA headers | headers absent | `''` stored in both capture columns; submission unaffected | N/A |
+| Over-long IP/UA | adversarial headers | Helpers slice to 64/512 before write; CHECK constraints never trip | N/A |
+| Pre-v1 rows | existing applications | `reference_contact_choice` stays NULL; capture columns `''` via DEFAULT | N/A |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
