+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given the migrations run from a reset DB, when they apply, then the enum value exists and the three columns exist with their bounds/CHECK, all idempotent.
+- Given an attested submission, when the transaction commits, then the app row carries choice='attested' + IP/UA, and exactly one `reference_contact_attestation` ack row exists with the current `policy_version`.
+- Given a declined submission, when the transaction commits, then choice='declined', NO attestation row exists, and the application submits normally (confirmation path).
+- Given a missing/empty/tampered choice, when validation runs, then submission fails with the choice error and zero application/ack rows persist.
+- Given the detail payload, when an application with a choice is fetched, then `reference_contact_choice` is present ('attested'/'declined'/null); IP/UA appear nowhere in the payload.
+- Given any code/copy/comment naming this record, when reviewed, then attestation/acknowledgement vocabulary is used — "consent" never appears in relation to it.
