+## Spec Change Log
+
+## Design Notes
+
+- Insert-layer guard: `validate_form` is the gate, but `insert_application_row` matches the choice exhaustively — anything other than the two literals aborts the tx via `HandlerLogicError`. A silently coerced 'declined' would fabricate a choice the applicant never made (A4's whole point is honest declined-vs-NULL distinction).
+- Shared type carries only `reference_contact_choice`: AD-11's boundary rule ("never leak raw IPs to the landlord payload") keeps the capture columns server-side; RC3.7 reads them via SQL directly.
+- Existing ack-count tests (no_guarantor 2, with_guarantor 3, co_applicant 3) keep their counts by giving `apply_form_fixture_values` a `choice` parameter defaulting to declined; the attested path gets its own dedicated tests.
+
+## Verification
+
+**Commands:**
+- `make test-db-up && make test-db-reset` -- full migration chain replays cleanly from reset
+- `bash run_squirrel.sh` -- generated query code in sync, no diff after regen
+- `make test-shared` -- green (codec tests)
+- `make test-server` -- green (unit tests)
+- `make test-integration` -- green (attested/declined/missing-choice + updated ack-count tests)
+- `cd server && gleam format --check src test` (and `shared`) -- formatting clean
+
+**Manual checks (if no CLI):**
+- `git grep -in "consent" -- server/src/application shared/src/shared | grep -i reference` returns nothing attestation-related (vocabulary sweep, excluding the pre-existing `consent_type` type name and unrelated GDPR consent code).
